# Agent Skills

Skills live in `.github/skills/` and are mirrored at `.cursor/skills/` for Cursor. **Edit skills only under `.github/skills/`** so GitHub Copilot and Cursor stay in sync.

When a task matches a skill, read and follow that skill's `SKILL.md` before proceeding:

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `create-habit` | Creating habits, workflows, or YAML frontends |
| `create-bit` | Creating bits, actions, or triggers |
| `server-cortex-mode` | Node.js Cortex server / backend work — not Tauri |
| `tauri-app-mode` | Tauri native app work — not Cortex server |
| `manage-admin-mode` | `@ha-bits/admin` package |
| `hub-mode` | `@codenteam/hub` package |
| `app-publishing` | iOS/Android/macOS builds, signing, store uploads |
| `record-browser-demo` | Recording headed browser tutorial videos (WebM) via Browser DevTools MCP |

`server-cortex-mode` and `tauri-app-mode` are mutually exclusive — pick one based on the runtime target.

## MCP Servers

Project MCP config lives at `.cursor/mcp.json` (Cursor), mirrored at `.mcp.json` (root) and `.vscode/mcp.json` (VS Code). **Edit `.cursor/mcp.json` first**, then keep the others in sync if needed.

| Server | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `habits-mcp` | Full Habits MCP server (91 tools): admin, Cortex, Tauri WebDriver, shell commands. Entry: `packages/manage/forge/src/mcp/index.ts` → `mcp.ts` |
| `wdio-mcp` | Generic WebDriver automation |
| `chrome-devtools` | Chrome DevTools debugging |

Tauri app tools (`run_app`, `pack_habit`, `run_workflow`, etc.) live in `packages/manage/forge/src/mcp/tauri-commands.ts` and are exposed via `habits-mcp`.

After changing MCP config, restart Cursor (Settings → MCP) so servers reload.
